// RHYTHM BANKRUPTCY — IN THE RED — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// RHYTHM BANKRUPTCY as Chicago acid house — a game alternate of rhythm, selectable
// from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// rhythm.js's own design taken literally: FIXED MELODIES, MOVING HARMONY. The ARP
// (cycle one) goes to a 303 two octaves down and is never transposed, while the
// doo-wop turnaround moves under it on a sub and a dry drawbar organ stabbing the
// off-beats — the original's own organ voice. A hand is on the cutoff: a resonant
// lowpass opens a step at a time, is shut for the breakdown and closes again at the
// end, so the loop seam is one continuous turn of the knob. The POPCORN HOOK (cycle
// two) is a house-piano riff, every note stacked into a chord; the breakdown
// re-harmonises it in A minor with a Bb Lydian bar. Acid two adds a second 303
// an octave up through a distortion — the title — and a robot reading the
// original's call figure.
// 
//   1–4    the machine alone — kick, hats, the 303 behind a shut filter (cabinet loop)
//   5–8    clap, open hat, sub and organ arrive; the knob starts to turn
//   9–24   acid one — the turnaround under the fixed 303; the piano riff from bar 17
//   25–32  breakdown — the hook re-harmonised: Am7 Fmaj7 Dm7 E7sus4 … Bbmaj7; no 303
//   33–36  build — the 303 back, the filter thrown open in four bars; roll, riser
//   37–52  ACID TWO — both 303s, the upper one in the red; piano riff; the robot
//   53–60  false ending — the machine alone for two bars, then everything
//   61–64  the knob turns back down; the loop returns to bar 5
// 
// THE BEAT CABINET'S CLOCK IS KEPT. 124 BPM straight, 4/4, phrases of four bars from
// bar 1, the kick on every quarter of every bar — the beat charts are laid off
// Audio.songBeat() mod 16. The loop is bars 5–64: 60 bars, the same length the
// original loops, a whole number of 16-beat chart loops.
// 
// 64 bars at 124. Written by work/local/_rhythm-remix-in-the-red.mjs through
// work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// SPOT FX (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-stops.mjs): the false ending on bar 53 cuts everything but the machine — kick, hats and both 303s.
//
// SPOT FX — MORE (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-more.mjs): the whole mix opens an eighth at a time over 33–36 and closes over 61–64 — the knob, on everything.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
